Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 01:51:09 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 23/27] Compressed engine: geometry coefficient tables when the
 packed ones exceed 4 MB

The packed tables (cg13) keep all six coefficient f4vectors of an operator for each update, 192 B per operator.
A graded mesh has many distinct operators (the SMA launch: 64410, 12.4 MB of packed tables), and the tables
then stream from memory next to the fields. Most of these operators differ in their edge lengths only: vi (iv)
carries the geometry, vv (ii) the material. The geometry layout keeps vi0 vi1 vi2 (iv0 iv1 iv2) per operator,
48 B in operator order, and a 16-bit index of the operator's vv0 vv1 vv2 (ii0 ii1 ii2) in a small table of the
distinct triplets: 100 B per operator for both updates instead of 192. The IJKN update loops take the six
coefficients from either layout (CoefPacked, CoefGeom in UpdateVoltages_IJKN_T / UpdateCurrents_IJKN_T): the
same values in the same operations (bit-identical). The geometry layout is chosen when the packed tables would
exceed 4 MB, and the packed one when more than 65535 distinct triplets exist; OPENEMS_COEF=packed or geom
chooses one. The fused sweep runs on either.

SMA launch (871 k cells), paired interleaved A/B, 8 rounds, other processes on 0.3-0.4 cores: x1.067
[1.021-1.116] at 8 threads, x1.033 with the automatic thread count, x1.025 at 4 (noisy), x0.992 at 1. The
other five models have at most 1.5 MB of packed tables and stay packed (geometry tables lose 2-5 % there at 4
threads).

